    "Description": "This is a kernel live patch module which can be loaded by the kpatch command line utility to modify the code of a running kernel.  This patch module is targeted for kernel-5.14.0-284.134.1.el9_2.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: RDMA/vmw_pvrdma: Fix double free on pvrdma_alloc_ucontext() error path (CVE-2026-46189)\n\n* kernel: net: ipv6: use-after-free in fib6_rule_suppress due to stale res-\u003ert6 pointer (CVE-2026-74581)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
